1
00:00:00,594 --> 00:00:02,269
Watch someone's eyes, and you know what they're

2
00:00:02,269 --> 00:00:03,342
thinking about.

3
00:00:03,342 --> 00:00:06,348
Every glance, every blink, says something.

4
00:00:06,554 --> 00:00:08,110
That's why machines are learning to read our

5
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:12,034
eyes. A headset sharpens only where you look.

6
00:00:15,024 --> 00:00:17,959
A car warns a driver whose eyes leave the road.

7
00:00:20,959 --> 00:00:23,375
People who can't speak type with their eyes.

8
00:00:26,365 --> 00:00:32,771
And a child's gaze can help doctors spot autism early.

9
00:00:33,766 --> 00:00:35,676
Every one of these systems has to learn from

10
00:00:35,676 --> 00:00:39,131
real faces, with eyes that move like real eyes.

11
00:00:39,131 --> 00:00:40,582
Filming people is slow

12
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,056
expensive and private.

13
00:00:42,056 --> 00:00:44,049
And most digital eyes look dead

14
00:00:44,049 --> 00:00:46,736
glassy, staring and robotic.

15
00:00:46,930 --> 00:00:48,746
This is Synthetic Eyes

16
00:00:48,746 --> 00:00:51,494
eye movement and virtual camera rendering, built

17
00:00:51,494 --> 00:00:53,947
brick by brick by Team Rocklef from SRM

18
00:00:53,947 --> 00:00:56,304
Institute of Science and Technology.

19
00:00:56,898 --> 00:00:59,669
Researchers built 3D head models like FLAME and

20
00:00:59,669 --> 00:01:02,476
GNM, and eye tools like UnityEyes.

21
00:01:02,476 --> 00:01:04,752
But the head models come without lifelike skin

22
00:01:04,752 --> 00:01:07,899
or eyes, and the eye tools only show the eye.

23
00:01:08,105 --> 00:01:10,735
So we built photoreal skin, living eyes and

24
00:01:10,735 --> 00:01:11,879
natural motion

25
00:01:11,879 --> 00:01:14,354
all driven by one Python script.

26
00:01:14,548 --> 00:01:16,506
Every texture is painted straight onto the

27
00:01:16,506 --> 00:01:20,385
head's own UV map, so it wraps on with no seams.

28
00:01:20,385 --> 00:01:23,039
Eight faces, of different ages and backgrounds

29
00:01:23,039 --> 00:01:25,987
with pores, freckles, wrinkles, and eyebrows

30
00:01:25,987 --> 00:01:27,589
drawn hair by hair.

31
00:01:27,783 --> 00:01:30,991
Each eye gets its own 4K iris, with fibres

32
00:01:30,991 --> 00:01:32,795
crypts and a ring of colour

33
00:01:32,795 --> 00:01:35,152
and a pupil that really traps the light.

34
00:01:35,358 --> 00:01:36,998
Then we check our own work

35
00:01:36,998 --> 00:01:39,439
every UV seam on the head is measured against

36
00:01:39,439 --> 00:01:41,314
the skin's natural detail.

37
00:01:41,314 --> 00:01:42,892
All eight sets pass.

38
00:01:43,099 --> 00:01:45,929
Type Left, Right, or Generate Motion, and the

39
00:01:45,929 --> 00:01:48,606
script renders the frames and the video.

40
00:01:48,606 --> 00:01:51,589
The eyes jump at real human speeds, settle

41
00:01:51,589 --> 00:01:53,122
drift, and blink

42
00:01:53,122 --> 00:01:55,422
fast to close, slower to open.

43
00:01:55,422 --> 00:01:56,860
The head follows a little

44
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:58,958
and the eyelids follow the eyes.

45
00:01:59,164 --> 00:02:01,287
The blend file plays a whole expression on

46
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:02,619
Blender's timeline

47
00:02:02,619 --> 00:02:05,768
surprise, a suspicious squint and an eye roll

48
00:02:05,768 --> 00:02:09,269
with eyelids, pupils and brows moving together.

49
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:11,999
Change the face with shape sliders, and the eyes

50
00:02:11,999 --> 00:02:14,014
stay perfectly in place.

51
00:02:14,863 --> 00:02:15,783
Under the hood

52
00:02:15,783 --> 00:02:18,531
the head model rebuilt in Python, expressions

53
00:02:18,531 --> 00:02:20,889
solved inside its own eye space

54
00:02:20,889 --> 00:02:23,660
textures baked through its UV map, and a control

55
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:24,686
wrapper to look

56
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,725
open the eyelids and blink.

57
00:02:26,919 --> 00:02:28,535
Compared with today's tools

58
00:02:28,535 --> 00:02:31,094
ours gives a whole photoreal face, a separate

59
00:02:31,094 --> 00:02:34,030
iris for each eye, human motion over time

60
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:36,140
and eyelids that follow the gaze.

61
00:02:36,346 --> 00:02:39,211
That opens the door to lifelike avatars, safer

62
00:02:39,211 --> 00:02:42,712
cars, better eye trackers, and medical research.

63
00:02:42,918 --> 00:02:45,666
Next, we'll carry the textures over to FLAME

64
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:48,225
add infrared headset cameras, and run it all in

65
00:02:48,225 --> 00:02:49,391
real time.

66
00:02:49,597 --> 00:02:51,683
Thank you, from Team Rocklef.

